Utility is a numerical representation of preferences. One can also think about the numerical representation of other abstract concepts. Here, we discuss a numerical representation of the concept “approximately the same” (see Luce (1956) and Rubinstein (1988)). For simplicity, let  $X$  be the interval  $[0, 1]$ .

