A choice correspondence  $C$  satisfies the *path independence* property if for every set  $A$  and a partition of  $A$  into  $A_1$  and  $A_2$  ( $A_1, A_2 \neq \emptyset$ ,  $A = A_1 \cup A_2$  and  $A_1 \cap A_2 = \emptyset$ ) we have  $C(A) = C(C(A_1) \cup C(A_2))$ . (The definition applies also to choice functions.)

