> **Image description:** A 2D coordinate graph with axes $x_1$ (horizontal) and $x_2$ (vertical). An indifference curve (convex to the origin) is tangent to a straight downward-sloping line at a point labeled $x$. A vector arrow labeled $v(x)$ points outward perpendicular to the tangent line at point $x$, representing the gradient or normal vector at the bundle $x$.

