Assume that the firm will receive a prize  $M$  if its report is actually correct and that the wage of each worker is  $w$ .

- c. Explain why it is true that if  $f$  is concave, then the firm chooses  $k^*$  so that the  $k^*$ th worker is the last one for whom marginal revenue exceeds the cost of a worker.
- d. Is this conclusion true in our case?

