Consider two possible approaches the decision maker can take:

*Approach 1:* He delays his decision until Monday (“Why bother with the decision now when I can make up my mind tomorrow?”).

*Approach 2:* He makes a contingent decision on Sunday regarding what he will do on Monday, that is, he decides what to do if he faces the choice between  $L_1$  and  $L_2$  and what to do if he faces the choice between  $L_3$  and  $L_4$  (“On Monday morning I will be too busy ...”).

