#### Problem B14. (Tel Aviv 2013 )

Consider a consumer in a world with two commodities. He has two continuous strictly-increasing evaluation functions  $v_1$  and  $v_2$  with a range  $[0, \infty)$ . Facing a budget set  $B(p_1, p_2, w)$ , the consumer compares  $v_1(w/p_1)$  and  $v_2(w/p_2)$  and spends all of his resources on the good that yields a higher evaluation (in the case of a tie he arbitrarily chooses one of the goods).

